From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 06:21:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi-qp: Stop the link training patterns when FRL training passes

When the sink clears its LTP request on every lane, link training has
passed and the link goes on to carry FRL data. frl_set_ltp() still writes
the lane pattern enables (FLT_CONFIG1[3:0] = 0xf) with pattern 0, so the
training pattern generator stays configured until the next training
cycle resets the register.

Clear FLT_CONFIG1 instead, as the Rockchip vendor driver does once
training passes.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
index 50794185563f..3728f4509b00 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
@@ -801,7 +801,14 @@ static int dw_hdmi_qp_bridge_frl_set_ltp(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	struct dw_hdmi_qp *hdmi = bridge->driver_private;
 	u32 flt_cfg;
 
-	flt_cfg = (ln3 << 16) | (ln2 << 12) | (ln1 << 8) | (ln0 << 4) | 0xf;
+	/*
+	 * No LTP requested on any lane means training passed: stop sending
+	 * link training patterns before the link carries FRL data.
+	 */
+	if (!ln0 && !ln1 && !ln2 && !ln3)
+		flt_cfg = 0;
+	else
+		flt_cfg = (ln3 << 16) | (ln2 << 12) | (ln1 << 8) | (ln0 << 4) | 0xf;
 
 	dw_hdmi_qp_write(hdmi, flt_cfg, FLT_CONFIG1);
 
